== Notes ==
* If Isaac already has full health when touching the bed, it will not activate the sleep sequence.
* Since they cannot hold Red Hearts, {{C|???}}, {{C|Black Judas}}, {{C|Tainted Judas}}, {{C|Tainted ???}}, {{C|Tainted Forgotten}} and {{C|Tainted Bethany}} will always gain 3 {{E|Soul Heart}}s when resting in a bed.
* Bedrooms are more likely to appear when playing as {{C|The Lost}}, {{C|Tainted Lost}}, and {{c|Tainted Forgotten}}.
* The bed provides no direct benefit for {{C|The Lost}} and {{C|Tainted Lost}}. Once activated, the sleep sequence will play, but afterward, there will be no notable effect.
** {{dlc+|a+}} This will still count towards unlocking the {{I|Blanket}}.{{dlc-}}
* Using a bed takes no game-tracked time. In spite of the pause in movement and slow fade out, the timer will display the same time when Isaac can move again as it did when he stopped moving.
* Sometimes the carpet can be obstructed by an [[urn]] or bed, making it impossible to reveal the trapdoor under it. Even if the urn is blown up, there will be no trapdoor under the carpet.
* {{dlc+|a+}} When using a bed with {{C|The Forgotten}}, he will get all {{E|Bone Heart}}s filled {{dlc|nr+}} and {{C|The Soul}} will receive 3 Soul Hearts.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} Soul hearts will be used to charge the {{i|Alabaster Box}} first, as if they were picked up normally.
** Although using the bed as {{C|The Lost}} / {{C|Tainted Lost}} does not give soul hearts as health, they will still count toward charging Alabaster Box.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} The {{s|Home}} floor will have two unique rooms similar to Bedrooms. One is Isaac's room, which has a clean bed, a carpet (with nothing underneath), and a {{e|Locked Chest}}. The other is Mom's room, which has {{e|Mom's Chest}} and an alternate bed, that triggers the sequence to {{e|Dogma}}'s fight once Isaac touches it.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|rnr+}} When playing {{C|Jacob and Esau}}, the bed will only heal the one that touched the bed.
** {{dlc|r+}} Beds will heal both characters.
* {{dlc|r+}} In [[multiplayer]], beds heal ''all'' players, not only the one who touched them.

